    "forecast": "low",
    "rationale": "Present design risk is low because the only data read is internal published policy text, the only reply sink is the authenticated requester's own chat session, hidden egress is explicitly constrained by the client, and general network egress is denied at the network layer and reportedly pen-tested. No untrusted source reaches a sensitive sink, and there are no write, delete, execute, spend, delegate, memory, or configuration capabilities. Manual validation was applied because scripts could not be run. Confidence is reduced for action provenance because logging details were not provided. The single most important forecast-sensitive control is ctrl.reply_bound_to_requester_session, but even with considered triggers the rating remains low for the reviewed design because no broader sink or data scope is evidenced today."
  },
